-- list_change_target_v1 learns a third kind of list: a flashcard deck; and
-- the deck itself gets an input kind (flashcard_deck_cards_v1, at the end).
--
-- First customer: the `flashcards.fix_giveaway_cards` mandate (Arman, 2026-10-02:
-- "have the ai modify the cards so that no card gives away the back of the
-- card"). The agent answers `list_change_proposal_v1` with
-- target {kind:"flashcard_deck", set_id}; the one proposal component lets the
-- deck's editor accept each card rewrite or all of them, and the port
-- (features/list-change-proposals/applyListChange.ts) writes through
-- fcService.updateCard.
--
-- Additive: one enum value and one nullable field. The envelope row is
-- re-emitted too because its $defs embed the target's schema. Payloads are
-- emitted verbatim by scripts/shape/emit-kind-rows.ts from the compiled floor in
-- features/content-ir/kinds/list-change-proposal.ts — never hand written.
-- Idempotent: each update runs only when the stored fingerprint differs.

